# One file, three contexts: Dockerfile, Dockerfile.admission and
# Dockerfile.controller all take the repository root as their context and all
# `COPY . .`, and docker reads this file by name regardless of -f.
#
# The build context is copied into the builder stage wholesale. target/ is a
# host-target build directory that the musl build must not inherit, and it is
# larger than everything else in the tree put together.
/target
.git
# dist/ is deliberately NOT here: the bpf object the image ships comes in
# through the context, and COPY failing on its absence is the check that an
# agent image cannot be built without a datapath.
